# Working trees are LF everywhere, including on Windows.
#
# At the ROOT because the rule has to cover every file in the repository, not
# just the two app directories that used to carry a copy each: this machine has
# `core.autocrlf=true`, which rewrites every file git checks out to CRLF, and
# Prettier's `endOfLine` default is `lf` — so on a fresh Windows clone the
# `shared format` and `root format` jobs failed on files nobody had touched.
# That is a checkout artefact, not a source defect, so it is fixed here rather
# than by relaxing the gate. `apps/back-end/.gitattributes` adds only the office
# fixtures it owns.
#
# After changing this file, run `git add --renormalize .` once so the index
# agrees with it.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.webp binary
*.avif binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.db binary
